FILE-13: reject TRIALS below 1 and initialise relerr

optionvalue() only required TRIALS to be above 0 and then stored
(int)y, so a value such as 0.5 gave MaxIter = 0. hydsolve() then ran no
trials: it returned the initial guess as the solution and left relerr
unset, which runhyd() went on to read. TRIALS below 1 is now rejected
with error 213, as EN_setoption(EN_TRIALS) already does. relerr is also
initialised in runhyd(), so hydsolve() never passes back an unset value
(it also stores it in hyd->RelativeError when the first trial fails).

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply FILE-13_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/hydraul.c b/src/hydraul.c
index fa96868..564659c 100755
--- a/src/hydraul.c
+++ b/src/hydraul.c
@@ -202,7 +202,7 @@ int   runhyd(Project *pr, long *t)
 
     int   iter;          // Iteration count
     int   errcode;       // Error code
-    double relerr;       // Solution accuracy
+    double relerr = 0.0; // Solution accuracy
 
     // Re-initialize leakage coeffs. if parameters have changed
     if (hyd->LeakageChanged)
